            <div xml:id="d846">

                <pb facs="0927" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg823"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Woodward Electoral Mission/165:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Nicaragua</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-09-15T18:00:00-04:00">September 15,
                            1932—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. Your 175, September 13, 2 p.m. After consultation with this Department the
                    Navy Department, in view of the fact that the Commander of the Guardia states
                    that escort for supplies for the electoral and marine personnel at Matagalpa
                    cannot be furnished by the Guardia, is authorizing the temporary employment of
                    marines to act as escort in this particular instance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
